From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:19:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aot_lift: ahead-of-time recompilation of AArch64 functions to
 x86_64 with Remill, branches, memory and calls

aot_lift.py lifts each function with remill-lift, generates the table of their addresses and builds one
shared library with aot_runtime.cpp: bounded guest memory (an access outside it is an explicit error),
indirect calls and jumps through the table (an unknown target is counted as a fallback request and stops
with its address until a JIT exists), direct bl as a linked call. An instruction Remill cannot lift is a
LiftError (address, word, text), an intrinsic the runtime lacks a LinkError.
Tests compare the fixture's branch, loop, nested-call and indirect functions, and 36 load/store forms
(unaligned, pre/post-indexed, pairs, sign extension), with the Unicorn AArch64 reference on all
registers, NZCV, sp and the guest memory. Skipped without REMILL_BUILD or unicorn.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: T3 of an AArch64 -> x86_64 recompilation (NX2Linux); new tool, runtime and tests, nothing in the host, loader or shader chain changes
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch feat/teo-t3-branches-memoire-appels)

